ALY.excerpt:
) A strong cold front will bring gusty winds, showers, and a few strong to potentially severe thunderstorms for Ulster, Dutchess and Litchfield Counties late this afternoon into early tonight.
) Continued gusty winds and unseasonably chilly conditions are expected tonight through Saturday. A coating to a few tenths of an inch of snow are possible in the high terrain late tonight into Saturday morning.
) Dry weather with temperatures moderating to near seasonable levels late Sunday into early next week.

BUF.excerpt:
) Periods of rain and gusty winds through this evening.
) Much colder tonight through Saturday night with a few wet snowflakes possible early Saturday morning.
) An extended period of dry and warmer weather begins Sunday and lasts most of next week.

CTP.excerpt:
) Scattered damaging winds possible this afternoon and evening
) Blustery and much turning much colder tonight and Saturday
) Frost and freeze conditions Saturday night into early Sunday

RLX.excerpt:
) A cold front brings showers, storms, and gusty winds today, followed by colder temperatures and continued breezes tonight.
) Widespread frost/freeze conditions are expected Saturday night into early Sunday morning.
) Quiet weather and a warming trend are expected next week.
